<item>
<title>[LIT-37] [E1] Spec-Driven Workflow Service (OpenSpec-style)</title>
<link>https://gorillalogic.atlassian.net/browse/LIT-37</link>
<project id="11390" key="LIT">Labs Initiatives Tracker</project>
<description><h2><a name="Summary"></a>Summary</h2> <p>The lifecycle <tt>explore → proposal → spec+design → tasks → apply → verify/archive</tt> as a reusable service. This is the skeleton of the agentic factory, and the substrate joining teams plug into. Every team inventing its own lifecycle produces artifacts that don't line up cross-team... adopting one explicit lifecycle makes cross-team review and audit feasible at speed.</p> <h2><a name="Pattern"></a>Pattern</h2> <p>A CLI + versioned spec storage. Per-phase hooks. Contract = a per-phase artifact schema. Plugin-friendly by target (Solo / Team / Scale). The call here is NOT to build a homegrown framework... it's to adopt an existing one and stop reinventing the spec → tasks → apply → verify chain. Observable signal = <tt>features_following_spec / features_total</tt>.</p> <h2><a name="Acceptancecriteria"></a>Acceptance criteria</h2> <ol> <li>Two different features follow the same lifecycle, with phase-visible artifacts.</li> <li>Each phase produces a versioned artifact against a schema.</li> <li>The lifecycle plugs into different targets without forking the workflow.</li> <li><b>Demo to Labs:</b> the working PoC is presented to the Labs team (plus a Lunch &amp; Learn, pending Mariana Santamaría's call).</li> <li><b>Article:</b> a piece is published laying out the architecture pattern, the PoC built, and the data collected (also pending Mariana Santamaría's call).</li> </ol> <h2><a name="References"></a>References</h2> <ul> <li><a href="https://github.com/Fission-AI/OpenSpec" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">OpenSpec</a> — the lifecycle to adopt.</li> </ul> </description>
